Reviewed-Daytona-Version: 0.218.0

Purpose
-------
This is PR 1 of the standalone Daytona interpreter simplification plan in
PRD-and-implementation-plan.md. It fixes two concrete adapter issues without
changing dependencies, public API schemas, Sandbox ownership, the broker
protocol, or the native DSPy RLM loop.

1. `_run_backend()` currently catches TypeError around the backend call and
   retries the same action without `on_stdout`. A TypeError raised after the
   backend has started, including from the stdout callback, can therefore
   replay side effects. This patch determines the supported call shape before
   execution, so one logical action is dispatched at most once locally.

2. `_public_output()` checks CodeInterpreterError before its subclass
   CodeExecutionError. This makes the recoverable public classification branch
   unreachable. The checks are reordered.

Scope
-----
Changed repository files: 2
New repository files: 0
New dependencies: 0
New configuration fields: 0

The signature-inspection compatibility branch is deliberately temporary. PR 3
standardizes every first-party InterpreterBackend.run() implementation on the
`on_stdout` keyword and BackendExecutionResult, after which this branch should
be deleted in favor of one direct typed call.

Regression cases added to the existing adapter test module
-----------------------------------------------------------
- backend-origin TypeError does not replay execution;
- stdout-callback TypeError does not replay execution;
- legacy, streaming, and **kwargs backend call shapes are selected before run;
- incompatible backend signature is rejected before execution;
- CodeExecutionError is projected as "Execution error";
- CodeInterpreterError is projected as "Execution failed".

